 "result": "I documented 12 repos this run. All the pushes went through.\n\nFour were backfills: `2026-11-24-green-fleetindex`, `2026-11-24-green-greenscreen`, `2026-11-25-blue-cliprig` and `2026-11-25-blue-manualrebuild`. Three updates got docs pushes: `ascend`, `spectral-engine` and `2026-11-16-orange-zion`. Five more needed only release jobs, because the developer had already written the changelog entries and READMEs. Those five are `datacenter-osint`, `topo-wars-server`, `pajamastan-warrants` and both `signal-snapshot` repos. I also refreshed the state for 20 repos whose only new commits were the scribe's own.\n\nNo new repo has a live site at its own name. They all answered 404, so those homepages are empty. No repo needed a root `vercel.json`.\n\nSix updates were deferred by the 12-repo cap: `field-twin`, `2026-11-22-orange-hubview`, `mohavetech-website`, `itchy-troll`, `2026-10-18-orange-testbed` and `2026-11-24-green-filecensus`. The `sudosilo`, `control-troll` and `heckle-troll` repos have no state entries. Earlier runs skipped them on purpose, so I did too, and no other backfills remain.\n\nThe profile page in `sudosilo/sudosilo` is updated. `scribe state` is pushed to control-troll main, with the new notes included. The release and settings work will happen when the `scribe-publish` workflow runs on that push. I did not check that it ran.",
